the-firm-as-one-program-lines-12 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-12 = cons "  - **PE1** Why abstraction costs today: the optimizer removes only work it can prove unnecessary, and proof stops at boundaries." (cons "    - **PE1.1** An unresolved indirect call, an unknown size, possible aliasing, an undischarged bounds check, a branch on a field of unknown range, a translation unit it cannot see." (cons "    - **PE1.2** Templates are zero-cost only when everything static is visible inside them; the decisive static knowledge lives in the protocol specification, the consumer's use of the message and the deployment, outside the code." nil))
